# Keeps that exist only so instrumentation can run against the minified debug build (#86, #2648).
#
# `androidx.test`'s runner loads inside the *app's* process and resolves against the *app's*
# classloader, so what it needs has to survive R8's pass over the app. The androidTest APK cannot
# supply it: those classes reach that APK as classpath, not as its own program classes, and no
# `-keep` in the test APK moves one into a dex.
#
# Without these, `AndroidJUnitRunner.onCreate` dies before test 1 with
# `NoClassDefFoundError: Lkotlin/LazyKt;`. AGP reports that as a crashed process with exit code 0,
# so the lane read green without running a test. See docs/device-smoke.md.
#
# Both are Kotlin facades the app never calls: R8 inlines every `lazy { }` call site and drops
# `LazyKt`, correctly. The pair is exact rather than a `kotlin.**` sweep.
#
# They live in `main`, not a debug-only source set, so the minified debug build and release minify
# against one identical set of rules. Two retained facade classes cost the shipped APK almost nothing.
-keep class kotlin.LazyKt { *; }
-keep class kotlin.coroutines.intrinsics.IntrinsicsKt { *; }
